 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded when the bundle is defined and replayed onto the app when the bundle is registered.\n\n**`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py`**\n- `Bundle(Scaffold)` (line 119) is the bundle class. `src/tessel/bundles.py` has a thin `Bundle(SansioBundle)` subclass on top of it.\n  - `Bundle.attach_route_rule()` (line 413) does not touch the app. It validates that the endpoint and view names have no dots, then calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))`.\n  - `Bundle.record()` (line 224) appends that lambda to `self.deferred_functions`.\n  - `Bundle.register(app, options)` (line 273) runs when the bundle is registered on the app. It calls `make_setup_state()` (line 246) to build a `BundleSetupState`, then loops over `self.deferred_functions` (line 334) calling each one with that state.\n- `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule()` (line 87) is what each deferred lambda ends up calling.\n  - It joins the bundle's `url_prefix` onto the rule.\n  - It applies the `subdomain` and merges the `url_defaults`.\n  - It prefixes the endpoint with `\"{name_prefix}.{name}.\"`.\n  - It then calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`, the app's real route registration.\n\nParent-to-child nesting goes through `Bundle.register_bundle()` (line 256), which stores the child so `register()` can register it with a combined prefix and name.",
